{"name":"Braid","hex":"#77675b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Braid","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Braid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Braid","blocks":[{"text":"A braid is a complex structure or pattern formed by interlacing three or more strands of flexible material such as textile yarns, wire, or hair.\nThe simplest and most common version is a flat, solid, three-stranded structure. More complex patterns can be constructed from an arbitrary number of strands to create a wider range of structures. The structure is usually long and narrow with each component strand functionally equivalent in zigzagging forward through the overlapping mass of the others. It can be compared with the process of weaving, which usually involves two separate perpendicular groups of strands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Braid_final_rot.jpg/330px-Braid_final_rot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Braid","wikidata":"Q320809"},{"title":"Braid (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Braid is an indie puzzle-platform video game developed by Number None. The game was originally released in August 2008 for the Xbox 360's Xbox Live Arcade service. Ports were developed and released for Microsoft Windows in April 2009, Mac OS X in May 2009, PlayStation 3 in November 2009, and Linux in December 2010. Jonathan Blow designed the game as a personal critique of contemporary trends in video game development. He self-funded the three-year project, working with webcomic artist David Hellman to develop the artwork."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Braidlogo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Braid_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q897376"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/M%C3%A4dchen_die_Haare_flechtend_1887.jpg/500px-M%C3%A4dchen_die_Haare_flechtend_1887.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/M%C3%A4dchen_die_Haare_flechtend_1887.jpg/500px-M%C3%A4dchen_die_Haare_flechtend_1887.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mädchen, die Haare flechtend (1887), by Albert Anker.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AM%C3%A4dchen_die_Haare_flechtend_1887.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Braid_StepBystep.jpg/500px-Braid_StepBystep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Braid_StepBystep.jpg/500px-Braid_StepBystep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A step-by-step creation of a basic braid using three strings","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABraid_StepBystep.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Braided_Stream_FairbanksTananaRiver.jpg/500px-Braided_Stream_FairbanksTananaRiver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Braided_Stream_FairbanksTananaRiver.jpg/500px-Braided_Stream_FairbanksTananaRiver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The braided streams of the Tanana River","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABraided_Stream_FairbanksTananaRiver.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/RG-59.jpg/330px-RG-59.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/73/RG-59.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or